\" Generated by script2man from auto-idrac-config
.TH auto-idrac-config 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-idrac-config - Set mode, network prefix size, and gateway for Dell iDRAC

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-idrac-config primary-Ethernet mode prefix-size gateway
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
primary-Ethernet    IP address of the primary Ethernet (Block1)
mode                "shared" or "dedicated" (check your iDRAC capabilities)
prefix-size         Number of bits in the network prefix
gateway             Network gateway IP address
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-idrac-config
command configures network access to a local Dell iDRAC platform.
It sets the address according to the cluster LAN scheme used
by SPCM (Simple Portable Cluster Manager),
https://github.com/outpaddling/SPCM.  In this scheme, the
available IP addresses are divided into four blocks.

.nf
.na
Block1  Primary Ethernet
Block2  LOM (Lights-out management)
Block3  High-speed network (e.g. Infiniband IP over IB)
Block4  Other
.ad
.fi

E.g., using a standard IPv4 192.168.0.0/16 network, this provides 16,384
addresses per block:

.nf
.na
Block1  192.168.0.1   - 192.168.63.255
Block2  192.168.64.0  - 192.168.127.255
Block3  192.168.128.0 - 192.168.191.255
Block4  192.168.192.0 - 192.168.255.255
.ad
.fi

The user provides the IP address of the primary Ethernet interface,
the desired iDRAC mode, network prefix size in bits, and the
network gateway.  The
.B auto-idrac-config
script retrieves the IP address of the given Block1 primary Ethernet
interface, calculates the corresponding address for the IDRAC
in Block2, and configures the iDRAC platform accordingly using
ipmitool(8).

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-idrac-config bce0 shared 24 192.168.0.1
auto-idrac-config em1 dedicated 16 192.168.1.1
.ad
.fi

.SH FILES
.nf
.na
/etc/hosts
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8), ipmitool(8)

